# Dashboard — Search, Filter & Sort

Core route: `POST /dashboard/filter` in `app/dashboard.py` → `filter_questions()`

## All Filter Parameters

| Param | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `subject` | string | Subject ID (e.g. `MATC`) |
| `source_type` | string | `DSE`, `CE`, `AL`, `QB` |
| `years` | list[int] | Multi-select, PP only |
| `section` | string | `A`, `Section I`, etc. |
| `topics` | list[int] | Topic IDs |
| `topic_mode` | `AND`\|`OR` | AND = question must have ALL selected |
| `subtopics` | list[int] | Subtopic IDs |
| `subtopic_mode` | `AND`\|`OR` | Same logic |
| `is_crosstopic` | bool | Include questions with topics as minor topics too |
| `is_crosssubtopic` | bool | Include questions with subtopics in M2M too |
| `chapters` | list[int] | Chapter IDs |
| `subchapters` | list[int] | Subchapter IDs |
| `levels` | list | `1`, `2`, `3`, and/or literal string `'null'` |
| `q_type` | string | `MC`, `CQ`, or `all` |
| `qid_search` | string | Direct QID search |
| `qid_strict` | bool | Strict: user controls pattern with `*` wildcard; Loose (default): tokenise and match in order |
| `qids` | string | Comma-separated explicit QID list. **Overrides all other filters** (only QIDs intersected with user-accessible subjects are returned). Set via `?qids=…` URL param from the Admin → DB Health anomaly view. The dashboard stores it in hidden input `#qidsInput` and shows a dismissible banner. |
| `ids` | string | Comma-separated explicit DB-id list (`Question.id`). **Overrides all other filters** (subject access still enforced). Powers the **Show Selected Only** toggle: the frontend writes `selectedQuestions` into hidden `#idsInput` and submits the filter form so the user paginates through their FULL selection regardless of the sidebar filter. Mutually exclusive with `qids` (qids wins if both set). |
| `page` | int | Page number (default 1) |
| `page_size` | int | 10, 20, 50, or 100 (default 20) |
| `version_priority` | comma string | Ordered version preference for card previews (e.g. `EN,CH,BI,ENO,CHO`); top wins. Legacy `preview_language` (`EN`/`CH`) still accepted and converted via `parse_version_priority()` |
| `sort_config` | JSON string | Array of `{field, direction}` objects |
| `sort_group_order` | JSON string | Optional manual block ordering `{fields:[...], order:[[id,...],...]}` for Topic/Subtopic/Chapter/Subchapter. Passed to `apply_multi_sort(..., group_order=)`. Ignored unless `fields` match the grouping fields in `sort_config` |

## Topic/Subtopic AND Logic
In AND mode, each selected topic must appear as **major OR any minor topic** (since a question can only have one major topic). The filter loops and applies one `.filter()` call per topic ID.

## QID Search Logic
- **Loose mode** (default): normalises to uppercase alphanumeric tokens, builds `%TOKEN1%TOKEN2%` LIKE pattern
- **Strict mode**: user writes the pattern directly; `*` maps to SQL `%`; no wildcards means substring match
- QID search and the `qids` list both apply at the start of the query
- `qids` (exact list) wins over `qid_search` (pattern) when both are present and **explicitly nulls out the other filter variables** so subject/topic/etc. blocks become no-ops

## Sorting
Uses `apply_multi_sort()` from `app/utils.py`. Multi-level: `[{field, direction}, ...]`.  
Available sort fields defined in `SORT_FIELDS` dict in `utils.py`:  
`qid`, `year`, `level`, `topic`, `subtopic`, `source`, `section`, `q_type`, `correct_percentage`, `chapter`, `subchapter`, `created_time`

**Important**: Sorting is done **in Python** after fetching all results from DB (not via SQL ORDER BY). This is intentional to support natural sort (Q1, Q2, Q10 not Q1, Q10, Q2) and multi-field sorting with null-handling. Do not move sorting to SQLAlchemy without careful consideration.

Pagination is also done in Python (slice after sort).

### Manual block reordering
When `sort_config` contains a grouping field (`topic`/`subtopic`/`chapter`/`subchapter`), the **Reorder blocks** button in the Sort By panel opens a modal that `POST`s the current filter form + `group_fields` to `POST /dashboard/api/sort-groups` and renders the returned blocks (SortableJS). The chosen order is stored in hidden `#sortGroupOrderInput` (and `localStorage[oqb_sortGroupOrder]`), included in `getCurrentFilterValues()` as `sort_group_order`, and re-submitted. Stale orders are auto-cleared client-side when the grouping fields change. The shared query builder is `_build_filtered_query(params)` (used by both `filter_questions` and the sort-groups API). See `apply_multi_sort(..., group_order=)` + `enumerate_sort_groups` in `utils-sorting.mdc`.

## Session Storage
- `session['filter_params']` — current filter state
- `session['sort_config']` — current sort config
- `session['generator_question_ids']` — question IDs carried to generator

## HTMX Pattern
When `HX-Request` header is present → return `partials/question_list.html` fragment only.  
Full page requests → return complete `dashboard.html`.

## API Endpoints (all require login)
- `GET /dashboard/api/topics/<subject_id>` — topics for subject
- `GET /dashboard/api/subtopics?topic_ids=1,2&include_hidden=0&q_type=all` — subtopics with question counts
- `GET /dashboard/api/chapters/<subject_id>` — chapters for subject
- `GET /dashboard/api/subchapters?chapter_ids=1,2&include_hidden=0` — subchapters
- `GET /dashboard/api/years/<subject_id>/<source>` — available years
- `GET /dashboard/api/sections/<subject_id>/<source>` — available sections
- `GET /dashboard/api/asset/<asset_id>` — asset info
- `GET /dashboard/api/question/<id>/assets/<type>` — all parts for a question's asset type (legacy; image-centric)
- `GET /dashboard/api/question/<id>/preview/<type>?version_priority=EN,CH,BI,ENO,CHO` — **unified preview resolver** (legacy `?lang=EN` still accepted). Returns `{mode: 'image'|'html'|'download', format, version, parts/html/url, ...}`. Format priority: **IMG > MD > DOC**. Used by dashboard cards (lazy fetch for HTML/download), the preview modal (`previewAsset()`), and the in-browser MD render helpers in `templates/base.html`.
- `GET /dashboard/files/<path>` — serve raw asset file from SOURCE_PATH

## Asset Version Selection (Preview)
Assets are sorted by `(format_rank, version_rank, part_number)` where `version_rank = version_priority.index(asset.version)` and `version_priority` comes from the drag-to-reorder widget (default `EN,CH,BI,ENO,CHO`). The best `(format, version)` group wins (format priority IMG > MD > DOC), and all `part_number` parts for that group are returned together. The View-menu widget persists to `localStorage[oqb_versionPriority]` and re-triggers the HTMX filter on change.
